# /sdd-purge

Purpose:
  Audit and clean AI provenance marks from generated artifacts.
  Bridges SDDRA to watermarks-remover service for Layer A (deterministic Unicode)
  and Layer Files (C2PA, EXIF, XMP, doc-provenance) hygiene.

Owns: commands/sdd-purge.sdd

Description:
  Calls the watermarks-remover HTTP service to inspect and clean generated
  artifacts for hidden AI metadata. Operates in two modes:
  inspect (detect only) and clean (strip in place). Activate as post-write
  gate in C1 (Code Generation) and D1 (Documentation) arms, and as
  pre-publish audit in DEP1 (Deploy) arm.

Usage:
  /sdd-purge
  /sdd-purge --file <path>
  /sdd-purge --directory <path>
  /sdd-purge --inspect
  /sdd-purge --layer <a|files|all>
  /sdd-purge --json

Options:
  --file        Target single file
  --directory   Target directory recursively
  --inspect     Detect only, do not mutate files
  --layer       Select detection layer: a (Unicode), files (metadata), all (default: all)
  --json        Output machine-readable JSON

Mode: READ_WRITE

Layers:
  layer_a: Invisible Unicode, exotic spaces, bidi, tag chars (deterministic)
  layer_files: C2PA, EXIF, XMP, doc-provenance metadata (deterministic)
  layer_b: Statistical text watermarks (best-effort, requires model backend)

ChainArmMapping:
  C1: post-write provenance check on generated code
  D1: post-write provenance check on generated docs
  DEP1: pre-publish provenance audit before deployment
  R1: review enhancement with provenance findings

Output:
  PROVENANCE AUDIT

    Files Scanned:    <count>
    Findings:         <count>
      Layer A:        <count>
      Layer Files:    <count>
    Decision:         PASS | WARN

  Findings Detail:
    [Layer A] file: notes.md:1
      kind: zero-width-space
      message: Invisible Unicode character detected
      remediation: Run /sdd-purge --file notes.md to clean

    [Layer Files] file: report.pdf:1
      kind: c2pa
      message: C2PA manifest found
      remediation: Run /sdd-purge --file report.pdf to clean metadata

Rules:
  [PRG-01] /sdd-purge MUST NOT modify files when --inspect is supplied.
  [PRG-02] /sdd-purge MUST fail open if the watermarks-remover service is unreachable.
  [PRG-03] Layer A and Layer Files findings MUST be treated as MEDIUM severity.
  [PRG-04] /sdd-purge MUST only scan files with registered artifact extensions.
  [PRG-05] Cleaned files MUST be written atomically; original preserved on failure.
  [PRG-06] /sdd-purge MUST emit OBS21 provenance_clean or OBS22 provenance_detected events.

